# Assignment 4.4 — Metadata & Page Setup

## Q1. Set UTF-8 for Character Encoding

**Answer:**

HTML file ke `<head>` section mein ye code add karo:

```html
<meta charset="UTF-8">
```

**Explanation:** UTF-8 ki help se webpage par English, Hindi aur special characters properly display hote hain.

## Q2. Add a Mobile Viewport Meta Tag

**Answer:**

```html
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
```

**Explanation:** Ye tag webpage ko mobile, tablet aur computer screens ke according properly display karne mein help karta hai.

## Q3. Write a Meaningful Title

**Answer:**

```html
<title>My College Portfolio</title>
```

**Explanation:** Title browser ke tab mein show hota hai. Har HTML page ka title us page ke content ke according hona chahiye.

Examples:

* Home page: `My Portfolio - Home`
* Registration page: `Student Registration Form`
* Marks table: `Student Marks Table`

## Q4. Add a Meta Description

**Answer:**

```html
<meta name="description" content="Welcome to my college portfolio website. Learn about my course, skills, projects, and interests.">
```

**Explanation:** Meta description webpage ke content ka short summary hota hai. Search engines ise search results mein dikha sakte hain.

## Q5. Add a Favicon

**Answer:**

HTML file ke `<head>` section mein ye code add karo:

```html
<link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="images/favicon.png">
```

**Explanation:** Favicon ek chhota icon hota hai jo browser tab mein page title ke paas dikhai deta hai.

**Important:** Project folder mein `images` naam ka folder banao aur uske andar `favicon.png` naam ki image rakho.

Folder structure:

```text
my-project/
│
├── index.html
├── style.css
│
└── images/
    └── favicon.png
```

Image ka naam aur path code se exactly match hona chahiye.

## Q6. Verify CSS Links and File Paths

**Answer:**

CSS file ko HTML se connect karne ke liye `<head>` section mein ye code add karo:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
```

**Explanation:** Agar HTML aur CSS files same folder mein hain, to `href="style.css"` use karo. Agar CSS file kisi doosre folder mein hai, to uska correct relative path likho.

Example folder structure:

```text
my-project/
│
├── index.html
├── css/
│   └── style.css
│
└── images/
    └── favicon.png
```

Is structure mein CSS link hoga:

```html
<link rel="stylesheet" href="css/style.css">
```

## Final Answer — Complete HTML Code

**File name:** `index.html`

Neeche diya gaya complete code copy karke `index.html` mein paste kar sakte ho.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <!-- Character Encoding -->
    <meta charset="UTF-8">

    <!-- Mobile Responsive Viewport -->
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">

    <!-- Page Title -->
    <title>My College Portfolio</title>

    <!-- Meta Description -->
    <meta name="description" content="Welcome to my college portfolio website. Learn about my course, skills, projects, and interests.">

    <!-- Favicon -->
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="images/favicon.png">

    <!-- External CSS -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
</head>

<body>

    <header>
        <h1>Welcome to My College Portfolio</h1>
        <p>This website contains information about my college course, skills, and projects.</p>
    </header>

    <main>
        <section>
            <h2>About My Course</h2>
            <p>I am a first-year Computer Science Engineering student.</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>My Skills</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>HTML</li>
                <li>CSS</li>
                <li>Java</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>My Goal</h2>
            <p>My goal is to improve my programming skills and build useful projects.</p>
        </section>
    </main>

    <footer>
        <p>&copy; 2026 My College Portfolio</p>
    </footer>

</body>

</html>
```

## Submission Requirements

Assignment submit karne se pehle ye checklist complete karo:

1. Apni HTML file mein UTF-8 encoding add karo.
2. Mobile viewport meta tag add karo.
3. Meaningful page title likho.
4. Meta description add karo.
5. `images/favicon.png` file add karo.
6. CSS file ka correct path check karo.
7. HTML file browser mein open karo.
8. Browser tab mein favicon dikhne ka screenshot lo.
9. Updated HTML file aur metadata code submit karo.

**Note:** Agar favicon turant show nahi hota, to image ka path aur filename check karo. Browser refresh karo; zarurat pade to hard refresh bhi try karo.
